^SAMPLE = GSM3717977
!Sample_title = scRNA-seq_p12: Single cell murine p12 subcutaneous WAT SVF
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM3717977
!Sample_status = Public on May 01 2019
!Sample_submission_date = Apr 11 2019
!Sample_last_update_date = May 02 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = C57BL/6 mice
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = gender: pooled male and female
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: Subcutaneous WAT (inguinal + axillary)
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = developmental stage: p12
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Tissues were manually minced, digested with Collagenase D and Dispase II at 37C for 45 min. For both mouse and human studies stromal vascular cells were isolated and flow sorted with gating to isolate single cells away from debris, doublets, and dead cells.  For the p12 pups (pooled male and female C57BL/6) and human single cell study, the cells were further gated against CD45 to exclude leukocytes.  For the adult mouse thermoneutral (pooled male 129S6/SvEvTac) sample CD45 cells were segregated and remixed with the SVC cells at a ratio of approximately 20% of the total cells.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The sorted cells were loaded onto a GemCode instrument (10x Genomics, Pleasanton, CA, USA) to generate single-cell barcoded droplets (GEMs) according to the manufacture’s protocol using the 10x Single Cell 3’ v2 chemistry.
!Sample_description = 10X Genomics Single Cell RNA-Seq
!Sample_data_processing = Basecalling via illumina software after
!Sample_data_processing = The Cell Ranger Single Cell Software Suite v.2.0.1 (mouse studies) or v.3.0.1 (human studies) was used to perform sample de-multiplexing, alignment, filtering, and UMI counting (https://support.10xgenomics.com/single-cell-gene-expression/software/pipelines/latest/what-is-cell-ranger). Data were analyzed with the default settings for these pipelines.
!Sample_data_processing = Clustering and gene expression were visualized with the Seurat package (version 3.0, https://satijalab.org/seurat/) on R Studio (https://www.rstudio.com).  Cells were first filtered to have > 500 detected genes and less than 5% of total UMIs mapping to the mitochondrial genome
!Sample_data_processing = Clusters with very few cells were filtered before downstream analysis.   Data was scaled to mitigate the effects of the following variables number of genes detected per cell, percent mitochondrial reads and cell cycle phase.
!Sample_data_processing = Dimensionality reduction was performed using the T-stochastic Neighboring Embedding method (t-SNE) using Seurat. Differential gene expression analysis between clusters was performed using the Seurat function FindMarkers using the wilcox test.  Violin plots, heatmap and individual tSNE plots for the given genes were generated using the Seurat toolkit ‘VlnPlot’, ‘DoHeatmap’ and ‘FeaturePlot’ functions respectively.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Cellranger barcodes and gene count matrices
!Sample_platform_id = GPL17021
!Sample_contact_name = Patrick,,Seale
!Sample_contact_email = sealep@pennmedicine.upenn.edu
!Sample_contact_institute = University of Pennsylvania
!Sample_contact_address = Smilow Center 3400 Civic Center Blvd. 1
!Sample_contact_city = Philadelphia
!Sample_contact_state = PA
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 19104
!Sample_contact_country = USA
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina HiSeq 2500
!Sample_library_selection = cDNA
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic
!Sample_library_strategy = RNA-Seq
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN11397492
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX5692096
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM3717nnn/GSM3717977/suppl/GSM3717977_SCmurinep12_barcodes.tsv.gz
!Sample_supplementary_file_2 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM3717nnn/GSM3717977/suppl/GSM3717977_SCmurinep12_genes.tsv.gz
!Sample_supplementary_file_3 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM3717nnn/GSM3717977/suppl/GSM3717977_SCmurinep12_matrix.mtx.gz
!Sample_series_id = GSE128889
